<template><div class="stack"><div class="split grow"><div class="col"><h2>Research implementation</h2><div class="steps"><article><span>01</span><div><h3>PyTorch + learned LUTs</h3><p>Differentiable representation training and image rendering.</p></div></article><article><span>02</span><div><h3>Transformer + image encoder</h3><p>Context from the query and paired historical examples. Audited source uses a pretrained ConvNeXt V2 backbone.</p></div></article><article><span>03</span><div><h3>nflows</h3><p>Conditional rational-quadratic spline coupling and invertible density estimation.</p></div></article></div></div><div class="col"><h2>Presentation and collaboration</h2><div class="steps"><article><span>01</span><div><h3>Slidev + Vue + Three.js</h3><p>Interactive diagrams, data views and a 3D distribution explanation.</p></div></article><article><span>02</span><div><h3>Playwright + GitHub Actions / Pages</h3><p>Browser verification and the existing presentation delivery workflow.</p></div></article><article><span>03</span><div><h3>GitHub, Zoom and WeChat</h3><p>Version control and reported client/team coordination.</p></div></article></div></div></div><p class="note">Research code and presentation code serve different deliverables. The presentation visualisations do not run the neural network in the browser.</p></div></template>
